# Stage 6 right clamp (D-075 visibility rule; game-design.md Stage 6
# "Difficulty and reach rules"): the solver route with RIGHT added to every
# frame that doesn't hold LEFT, so through the whole scroll Resi's hitbox
# stays at the right clamp (its left edge 242-243 px right of the camera
# until the scroll ends at ~4200). Measured on this replay (first frame any
# part of the enemy's hitbox is on screen -> first frame it reaches the
# clamp line, where she can be touched): swans #1-#3 63 frames (they
# trigger as soon as they are fully on screen, 20 frames in, hiss 32, then
# charge; the sprite shows ~5 frames before the hitbox), Gelsen #1-#3 81
# frames (60 frames hovering fully on screen, then the hunt), regatta boats
# #1-#3 85 frames (fully on screen 30 frames in, then the 60-frame start).
# Swans and Gelsen never touch her here (she dives under the swans and
# outswims the Gelsen as the solver does); regatta #2 bounces her off its
# masthead at 3955, 87 frames after it showed. No hurt, no death.
level  = wolfgangsee
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 no_event=Hurt
